            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}.rn{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,"SF Pro Text",sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;margin:4px 2px}.rn h1{font-size:16px;margin:0 0 10px}.rn h2{font-size:14px;margin:14px 0 6px}.rn ul{margin:6px 0;padding-left:20px}.rn li{margin-bottom:7px}.rn code{font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12px}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.rn{color:#e8e8ed}}</style><div class="rn"><h1>Rein 0.8.15</h1>
<ul>
<li><b>The crash fix, properly this time.</b> 0.8.14 guarded one bad value macOS can report for the tidy divider's window, but your Mac produced a second kind we've now seen in the wild (a window id too large to be real). Rein now treats every impossible window id as "skip this pass" instead of trusting the system's paperwork — there is no longer any code path that can trip over it.</li>
</ul></div>
]]></description>
